From a0972a77269b0a2e9062e7b944c8c6d49d8a350f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 14:42:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix duplicate job execution, require dedicated secrets, add
 tests

- api/jobs/run.ts: claim execution jobs with a single conditional UPDATE
  instead of select-then-update. Vercel cron and the GitHub Actions
  workflow both poll this endpoint every 5 minutes; the old select+update
  pattern let two overlapping runs claim and execute the same job twice
  (duplicate emails, calendar invites, vendor orders). Also switch the
  CRON_SECRET check to a timing-safe comparison.
- server/credentials.ts: CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY and OAUTH_STATE_SECRET
  are now required and no longer silently fall back to
  SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. Reusing one secret for three purposes meant a
  leak of any one compromised all three. Requires adding both keys in
  Vercel (see .env.example / README) before this deploys.
- Fix two pre-existing TypeScript errors (api/commands/interpret.ts,
  src/components/TaurantoServiceFan.tsx) that were failing `npm run
  typecheck`, which verify-ui-build.yml runs on every push to main.
- app.json: remove duplicated Android RECORD_AUDIO/MODIFY_AUDIO_SETTINGS
  permission entries.
- package.json: drop the unused `vite`-based "dev" script (no vite config
  or import exists anywhere in the app); add vitest/eslint/prettier as
  devDependencies with test/lint/format scripts.
- Add vitest tests for the pure command-validation, impact-plan, and
  approval-threshold logic in server/operations.ts, and for the
  credential-encryption/OAuth-state-signing logic in
  server/credentials.ts.
- README.md: correct the auth section to describe the email+password flow
  that AuthScreen.tsx actually implements (was documented as magic-link),
  and document the two new required secrets.

Verified locally: npm run typecheck, npx vitest run (19 passing), and
npm run build:web all succeed after these changes.

